  "nl_text": "The rschema_0361 database is designed to manage information about restaurants and their associated reviews, dishes, and replies. At the heart of the database is the Restaurant table, which stores details about each restaurant, including its address, average cost, business hours, name, phone number, and a unique identifier known as the Restaurant ID. The User_review table holds reviews written by users, containing the actual photos, dining time, rating, a unique review ID, and the content of the review. The Dish table is used to store information about the dishes served at each restaurant, including their category, description, image URL, monthly sales, name, price, and satisfaction rate, with each dish linked to its parent restaurant through the Restaurant ID. The Review_reply table allows users to respond to existing reviews, storing the reply content, reply time, and the ID of the review being replied to. The Restaurant ID in the Dish table is a foreign key referencing the Restaurant ID in the Restaurant table, ensuring data consistency between the two tables, while the Review_ID_being_replied_to in the Review_reply table is a foreign key referencing the Review_ID in the User_review table, linking replies to their parent reviews.",
  "gold_question": "This is a restaurant recommendation system for managing restaurant information and recommending nearby restaurants. For basic restaurant information management, the system maintains restaurant basic information, including restaurant ID, name, address, phone number, business hours, and average cost per person. It records restaurant geographical location information including latitude and longitude coordinates, manages restaurant feature tags such as \"Sichuan cuisine\", \"hot pot\", \"family gathering\", etc., and tracks restaurant ratings and number of reviews. For dish management, the system records information about dishes offered by each restaurant, including dish ID, name, price, description, etc. It adds category tags to dishes such as \"signature dish\", \"best-seller\", \"new arrival\", etc., supports uploading dish images, and records dish satisfaction rate and monthly sales. For user review management, the system supports users to rate and review restaurants, recording review content, rating, dining time, and other information. It supports uploading actual dining photos, and allows restaurants to reply to reviews, including reply time and content.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0361.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0361\nCREATE TABLE `restaurant` (\n  `restaurant_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `average_cost` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `business_hours` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`restaurant_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_review` (\n  `review_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `restaurant_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `dining_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `rating` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `photos` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`review_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_review_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`restaurant_id`) REFERENCES `restaurant` (`restaurant_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `dish` (\n  `dish_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `restaurant_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text NOT NULL,\n  `image_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `monthly_sales` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `satisfaction_rate` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`dish_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `dish_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`restaurant_id`) REFERENCES `restaurant` (`restaurant_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `review_reply` (\n  `reply_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `review_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `reply_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `reply_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`reply_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `review_reply_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`review_id`) REFERENCES `user_review` (`review_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
